Increments or decrements the underlying iterator.

     Overload                              Equivalent to
     \fB(1)\fP      ++current ﻿; return *this;
     \fB(2)\fP      --current ﻿; return *this;
              move_iterator tmp = *this; ++current ﻿; return tmp;       \fI(until C++20)\fP
     \fB(3)\fP        * move_iterator tmp = *this; ++current ﻿; return tmp;
                  if Iter models forward_iterator                       \fI(since C++20)\fP
                * ++current; otherwise
     \fB(4)\fP      move_iterator tmp = *this; --current ﻿; return tmp;
     \fB(5)\fP      return move_iterator(current  + n);
     \fB(6)\fP      return move_iterator(current  - n);
     \fB(7)\fP      current  += n; return *this;
     \fB(8)\fP      current  -= n; return *this;

.SH Parameters

n - position relative to current location

.SH Return value

As described above.

